<!-- The vaeb motion-brief Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs; docs/EVAL-LOOP.md,
     "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}) at 12 pt (size 24 half points; no E.D. Va. rule
     sets a size, both filed exemplars use 12 pt); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch-body, double
     spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst
     pitch-single). Replaced or added here, as the typst template sets them: the three heading levels at the type size
     on the body pitch with no space of their own (level 1 centred bold, the filter types it in capitals; 2 bold; 3
     bold italic), "Numbered Paragraph" (LBR 7056-1(C): the number at the indent, a tab 1 in from the
     margin, the text; typst number-box), "Lettered" (the label at the indent, the text hanging at 1 in; typst
     letter-box). Letter page (LBR 5005-1(C)(3)), a 1.5 in top margin (LBR 5005-1(C)(3)), 1 in other margins, the page
     number centred in a single-pitch line whose box ends 0.5 in above the page edge (typst footer-distance). Cover,
     caption, signature and certificate of service carry their own spacing (docx/vaeb.lua). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
